hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1105","Chapter on drawing up ranks for fighting and dismounting, 1144 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara' say: So he dismounted and sought help - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he said: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib. Then he drew up his companions in ranks."
